1
00:00:07,269 --> 00:00:11,727
Over the past months my articles have
taken up one question after another.

2
00:00:11,807 --> 00:00:13,629
Cause without causal power.

3
00:00:13,709 --> 00:00:15,884
Continuity without a carrier.

4
00:00:15,964 --> 00:00:18,316
How identities form in the meeting.

5
00:00:18,396 --> 00:00:20,033
What a phenomenon is.

6
00:00:20,833 --> 00:00:25,010
Looking back over them, I see one
shape running through all of them.

7
00:00:25,842 --> 00:00:28,629
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

8
00:00:28,709 --> 00:00:32,900
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

9
00:00:33,718 --> 00:00:35,500
There are two halves to the work.

10
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:40,418
One half is negation: seeing that
nothing is found from its own side.

11
00:00:40,498 --> 00:00:46,437
The other half is formation: understanding
how a world without essence still appears.

12
00:00:46,517 --> 00:00:48,779
Vivid. Stable. Working.

13
00:00:49,597 --> 00:00:52,864
Start with negation, and
with what it has to face.

14
00:00:53,694 --> 00:00:58,465
One of the most important turns in
leaving a substantialist view is this.

15
00:00:58,545 --> 00:01:02,853
The things, the substrates,
and everything I took as given,

16
00:01:02,933 --> 00:01:08,682
undeniable and there from its own side,
turn out to be frameworks. I built them.

17
00:01:08,762 --> 00:01:11,689
And I grew so used to them
that I never questioned them.

18
00:01:12,514 --> 00:01:17,040
Substantialism is not mainly a
theory anyone chooses to believe.

19
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:20,192
It is an innate, default
way of perceiving.

20
00:01:20,272 --> 00:01:23,467
It assumes that separate
nouns exist first,

21
00:01:23,547 --> 00:01:28,104
from their own side, and enter
into relations only afterwards.

22
00:01:28,921 --> 00:01:34,921
Ordinary grammar supports this every time
I speak. The wind blows. The person walks.

23
00:01:35,048 --> 00:01:39,357
Each sentence slips in a fixed
bearer, standing behind the action.

24
00:01:39,437 --> 00:01:44,887
Because the habit is so reliable, the act
of naming disappears into what is named.

25
00:01:44,967 --> 00:01:49,334
A convention feels like a fact
standing outside any framework.

26
00:01:50,141 --> 00:01:52,398
Direct experience is never like that.

27
00:01:52,478 --> 00:01:54,436
The flashing is the lightning.

28
00:01:54,516 --> 00:01:56,161
The blowing is the wind.

29
00:01:56,241 --> 00:01:58,571
No seer stands behind the seeing.

30
00:01:59,385 --> 00:02:04,210
Nor is there a raw, unnamed given
lying underneath my concepts,

31
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:09,250
waiting to be labelled. Vividness and
naming are mixed through and through.

32
00:02:09,330 --> 00:02:13,562
There is no seam between them, and
no unnamed floor at the bottom.

33
00:02:14,365 --> 00:02:17,423
Modern physics points
in a similar direction.

34
00:02:17,503 --> 00:02:22,192
Again and again, what was supposed to be
the bottom layer turns out to be defined

35
00:02:22,272 --> 00:02:27,210
by interaction and relation, rather
than by fixed properties of its own.

36
00:02:28,038 --> 00:02:32,446
But this view does not rest on
physics, and does not need it as proof.

37
00:02:32,563 --> 00:02:35,852
Physical theories are
themselves valid frameworks.

38
00:02:35,932 --> 00:02:39,661
Reliable within their
domains. Open to revision.

39
00:02:40,461 --> 00:02:44,049
More basically, a fixed
nature does not hold together.

40
00:02:44,129 --> 00:02:49,063
Anything proposed as standing on
its own undermines itself at once.

41
00:02:49,143 --> 00:02:53,397
To pick it out at all needs
contrast, context and naming:

42
00:02:53,477 --> 00:02:56,223
the very dependencies it claims to escape.

43
00:02:56,303 --> 00:03:01,481
And a thing with a fixed, independent
nature could never depend on conditions.

44
00:03:01,561 --> 00:03:04,611
It could never change.
It could never interact.

45
00:03:05,425 --> 00:03:08,904
Leaving this habit is not a
one-time change of opinion.

46
00:03:08,984 --> 00:03:13,524
The old picture comes back quietly
the moment attention is off duty.

47
00:03:13,604 --> 00:03:17,410
In my own experience, three
strands have to work together,

48
00:03:17,490 --> 00:03:20,811
again and again, each checking the others.

49
00:03:21,642 --> 00:03:25,140
The first strand: confirm
it in direct experience.

50
00:03:25,953 --> 00:03:29,555
Agreeing with dependency in
theory changes very little.

51
00:03:29,635 --> 00:03:35,334
It has to be seen directly, many times,
until it is no longer just an idea.

52
00:03:35,423 --> 00:03:41,423
For me this began with anatta, no-self:
looking for a seer behind the seeing,

53
00:03:41,523 --> 00:03:44,582
a hearer behind the
hearing, and finding none.

54
00:03:44,662 --> 00:03:49,736
Then it went on with ordinary
objects. A phone. A cup. A tree.

55
00:03:50,570 --> 00:03:52,814
But experience alone has a limit.

56
00:03:52,894 --> 00:03:55,776
Experience can become deeply non-dual.

57
00:03:55,856 --> 00:03:59,430
A taste of clarity, of
presence with no centre.

58
00:03:59,510 --> 00:04:03,072
And yet the framework that reads
it can stay substantialist.

59
00:04:03,152 --> 00:04:08,031
Then the habit quietly turns a genuine
taste back into a hidden ground.

60
00:04:08,111 --> 00:04:11,577
Solid things are simply
replaced by a subtler substrate.

61
00:04:11,657 --> 00:04:13,384
A universal Awareness.

62
00:04:13,464 --> 00:04:15,359
A Presence with a capital P.

63
00:04:16,182 --> 00:04:19,354
The second strand: equip
the view with tools.

64
00:04:20,157 --> 00:04:25,009
Analytical tools bring thinking in line
with what experience has already shown.

65
00:04:25,089 --> 00:04:30,145
Some are simple and easy to carry,
like the chariot of the monk Nāgasena.

66
00:04:30,225 --> 00:04:32,971
Look for the chariot in
the wheels, the axle,

67
00:04:33,051 --> 00:04:35,634
the frame, and it is not found there.

68
00:04:35,714 --> 00:04:38,079
Not in the parts, not apart from them.

69
00:04:38,159 --> 00:04:43,935
Some tools are thorough and exacting,
like Candrakīrti's sevenfold analysis,

70
00:04:44,015 --> 00:04:46,779
and Nāgārjuna's Middle Way verses.

71
00:04:47,593 --> 00:04:50,597
The analysis has to
work as a pure negation.

72
00:04:50,677 --> 00:04:55,108
It removes a nature of its own,
and puts nothing in its place.

73
00:04:55,188 --> 00:04:59,741
Otherwise the habit simply moves
to a subtler level. A void.

74
00:04:59,821 --> 00:05:02,988
A dynamic process. A web of relations.

75
00:05:03,068 --> 00:05:07,150
Or a store of possibilities,
quietly standing underneath.

76
00:05:07,962 --> 00:05:11,297
The third strand: taste
the gradual loosening.

77
00:05:12,105 --> 00:05:16,427
Whatever is taken to exist from its own
side is gripped with the tightness that

78
00:05:16,507 --> 00:05:18,166
solidity invites.

79
00:05:18,246 --> 00:05:21,604
As view and experience
keep confirming each other,

80
00:05:21,684 --> 00:05:24,267
that grip loosens. Gradually.

81
00:05:24,347 --> 00:05:28,143
The emotional grasping, and the
subtler grasping of the mind.

82
00:05:28,957 --> 00:05:31,784
What is left is not a
special state to be guarded.

83
00:05:31,864 --> 00:05:34,298
Trying to keep it would
bring the fixing back.

84
00:05:34,378 --> 00:05:37,735
Instead, mind and matter
lose their felt weight.

85
00:05:37,815 --> 00:05:40,878
They become light, vivid, and workable.

86
00:05:41,681 --> 00:05:46,768
And here is the turn. Relentless
negation alone is only half the story.

87
00:05:47,589 --> 00:05:51,870
Negation targets a fixed nature,
inside the old framework.

88
00:05:51,950 --> 00:05:54,384
If I stop there, I am left wondering.

89
00:05:54,464 --> 00:05:58,043
If these vivid appearances are
not things, then what are they?

90
00:05:58,849 --> 00:06:00,807
The other half is formation.

91
00:06:00,887 --> 00:06:04,217
How a world empty of
essence still appears vivid,

92
00:06:04,297 --> 00:06:06,178
stable and workable.

93
00:06:06,989 --> 00:06:11,718
In this view, a phenomenon is a vivid
appearing that is not found when looked

94
00:06:11,798 --> 00:06:14,816
for, even while it appears so vividly.

95
00:06:14,896 --> 00:06:18,394
Every appearance has three
features, at the same time.

96
00:06:19,209 --> 00:06:23,164
It is vivid and clear. Nothing
is dimmed or taken away.

97
00:06:23,244 --> 00:06:26,384
Its clarity belongs to
the appearing itself.

98
00:06:26,464 --> 00:06:28,232
A sound is clear as sound.

99
00:06:28,312 --> 00:06:30,270
A colour is vivid as colour.

100
00:06:30,350 --> 00:06:33,440
No witness behind it is
needed to light it up.

101
00:06:34,261 --> 00:06:40,261
It is not found. Searched for, it
has no core, no edge, no location.

102
00:06:40,388 --> 00:06:44,221
Not out there in the world.
Not in here, in a private mind.

103
00:06:44,301 --> 00:06:48,207
And not even nowhere, since
nowhere is just one more place.

104
00:06:49,025 --> 00:06:52,586
And it is dependently arisen,
and validly functioning.

105
00:06:52,666 --> 00:06:56,721
It shows up only when its conditions
meet. And it works completely.

106
00:06:57,538 --> 00:07:00,991
This third point is the one I
have had to come back to most.

107
00:07:01,071 --> 00:07:03,043
At first it sounds so strange.

108
00:07:03,123 --> 00:07:06,004
Habit equates being there
with being independent.

109
00:07:06,084 --> 00:07:09,822
It hears naming as a thin
sticker on a thing already there.

110
00:07:09,902 --> 00:07:13,532
It pictures causes as one
substance pushing another.

111
00:07:13,612 --> 00:07:16,294
So empty sounds flimsy. Ghostly.

112
00:07:17,126 --> 00:07:19,030
But empty does not mean weak.

113
00:07:19,110 --> 00:07:23,174
A car with no essence can still
injure you. Medicine still heals.

114
00:07:23,254 --> 00:07:25,094
A cup still holds hot tea.

115
00:07:25,901 --> 00:07:28,565
Take an apple, tossed from hand to hand.

116
00:07:28,645 --> 00:07:32,478
At once, habit supplies
the impression of a hard,

117
00:07:32,558 --> 00:07:34,820
heavy thing standing on its own.

118
00:07:35,625 --> 00:07:39,770
Yet when I look closely, the apple is
not found apart from the streams of

119
00:07:39,850 --> 00:07:43,008
consciousness. And it is
not made by them either.

120
00:07:43,826 --> 00:07:49,154
Hardness, coolness and weight arise
only as touch meets skin and fruit.

121
00:07:49,234 --> 00:07:53,379
The red shifts to orange under
candlelight, and to grey at dusk.

122
00:07:53,459 --> 00:07:56,509
It arises with light, eye and attention.

123
00:07:57,329 --> 00:08:01,067
When the habitual knot is
untied, nothing is missing.

124
00:08:01,147 --> 00:08:05,591
The apple can still be tossed.
Still eaten. It still nourishes me.

125
00:08:05,671 --> 00:08:10,645
Its solidity and its effects arise
because this vivid pattern meets hands,

126
00:08:10,725 --> 00:08:13,408
gravity and bodies, reliably.

127
00:08:14,229 --> 00:08:16,228
One guardrail stays in place.

128
00:08:16,308 --> 00:08:20,344
Consciousness is not a new floor
in here, producing the apple.

129
00:08:20,424 --> 00:08:24,081
Mind and matter are two cuts
in the same vivid appearing.

130
00:08:24,161 --> 00:08:28,474
Neither is the substrate underneath
the other. Both are named together.

131
00:08:29,294 --> 00:08:33,702
The same two halves run through the
rest of my recent work. Briefly, then.

132
00:08:34,571 --> 00:08:39,437
First, cause. Strike a match, and
slow the film down as far as you like.

133
00:08:39,517 --> 00:08:42,018
At every frame, something is happening.

134
00:08:42,098 --> 00:08:46,203
At no frame does a finished
flame cross over from nowhere.

135
00:08:46,283 --> 00:08:50,175
And still, she lit the fire
at eight is perfectly valid.

136
00:08:50,985 --> 00:08:53,921
Causes work. Rice grows from rice seed.

137
00:08:54,001 --> 00:08:56,204
Bread without yeast stays flat.

138
00:08:56,284 --> 00:09:01,244
What is never found is a causal power: a
force sitting inside the cause from its

139
00:09:01,324 --> 00:09:04,985
own side, handed across
a gap to the effect.

140
00:09:05,810 --> 00:09:08,393
So I keep three senses of cause apart.

141
00:09:08,473 --> 00:09:11,464
A producer with its own power: refused.

142
00:09:11,544 --> 00:09:13,964
Conditions coming together: kept.

143
00:09:14,044 --> 00:09:18,013
A link that attention singles
out and names: kept too.

144
00:09:18,093 --> 00:09:20,948
Conditions are not a
basement under the appearing.

145
00:09:21,028 --> 00:09:24,901
Conditions are the appearing,
cut into parts for explaining,

146
00:09:24,981 --> 00:09:26,591
and for getting things done.

147
00:09:27,401 --> 00:09:32,946
When no gap and no producer are found, the
question of why anything appears at all is

148
00:09:33,026 --> 00:09:38,258
retired. What remains is called
spontaneous presence. Not uncaused.

149
00:09:38,338 --> 00:09:39,712
Not a hidden source.

150
00:09:39,792 --> 00:09:44,336
Just dependent arising itself,
met without the habit of fixing.

151
00:09:45,154 --> 00:09:46,936
Second, continuity.

152
00:09:47,016 --> 00:09:51,610
If nothing persists from its own side,
what carries me from this moment to the

153
00:09:51,690 --> 00:09:52,890
next?

154
00:09:53,486 --> 00:09:56,898
The question rests on a gap
that thought drew first.

155
00:09:56,978 --> 00:09:59,412
In the living moment it never comes up.

156
00:09:59,492 --> 00:10:01,205
Each moment is complete.

157
00:10:01,285 --> 00:10:03,556
And a carrier would never solve it anyway.

158
00:10:03,636 --> 00:10:06,232
Whatever links one moment to the carrier,

159
00:10:06,312 --> 00:10:10,979
and the carrier to the next, needs
bridges of its own. Without end.

160
00:10:11,789 --> 00:10:16,885
As Nāgārjuna says, whatever arises in
dependence on something is neither that

161
00:10:16,965 --> 00:10:19,766
very thing, nor wholly other than it.

162
00:10:19,846 --> 00:10:24,779
Like a lamp burning through the night,
continuity is named across moments that

163
00:10:24,859 --> 00:10:27,293
condition one another reliably.

164
00:10:27,373 --> 00:10:29,770
Nothing travels from one to the next.

165
00:10:30,585 --> 00:10:35,912
Nothing is lost. Memory, learning,
responsibility and karma hold.

166
00:10:35,992 --> 00:10:40,428
And nothing is fixed. Habits can
loosen. Character can change.

167
00:10:41,299 --> 00:10:43,488
Third, the words themselves.

168
00:10:43,568 --> 00:10:47,510
Both views use the same words,
so the words have to be sorted.

169
00:10:47,590 --> 00:10:53,257
Heard by the logic of substance, dependent
arising means things that already exist,

170
00:10:53,337 --> 00:10:55,227
linked in a vast web.

171
00:10:55,307 --> 00:11:00,866
Meant by the logic of dependency, it means
things identified only in dependence.

172
00:11:00,946 --> 00:11:05,517
Relation and what is related are
named together. Neither comes first.

173
00:11:06,329 --> 00:11:10,243
Emptiness, heard the first
way, is a blank void,

174
00:11:10,323 --> 00:11:12,933
or a hidden reservoir behind things.

175
00:11:13,013 --> 00:11:18,504
Meant the second way, it is simply
this: no nature of its own is found,

176
00:11:18,584 --> 00:11:21,222
in appearances that are vivid and working.

177
00:11:21,302 --> 00:11:23,423
And the word real is retired.

178
00:11:23,503 --> 00:11:25,189
Working, conventionally.

179
00:11:25,269 --> 00:11:28,019
Not found from its own side, ultimately.

180
00:11:28,821 --> 00:11:33,089
If things existed with fixed
natures, nothing could ever meet.

181
00:11:33,169 --> 00:11:35,874
Two things with sealed
edges could never touch.

182
00:11:35,954 --> 00:11:39,017
And if they merged, they
would collapse into one.

183
00:11:39,817 --> 00:11:42,984
In dependent arising,
meeting means something else.

184
00:11:43,064 --> 00:11:47,658
The two sides define each other
in one stroke. A hand touches ice.

185
00:11:47,738 --> 00:11:51,326
They meet, with no gap
crossed, and no fusion.

186
00:11:51,406 --> 00:11:53,940
And the meeting itself
is not a third thing.

187
00:11:54,749 --> 00:11:57,988
So, with both halves in
place, what has changed?

188
00:11:58,822 --> 00:12:01,106
Nothing has been taken
away from the world.

189
00:12:01,186 --> 00:12:03,230
And no new ground has been added.

190
00:12:04,045 --> 00:12:07,443
The apple is still red.
The car is still dangerous.

191
00:12:07,523 --> 00:12:09,332
The cup still holds hot tea.

192
00:12:09,412 --> 00:12:11,442
A friend's voice is still warm.

193
00:12:12,257 --> 00:12:15,021
What has gone is only the
floor that was never there.

194
00:12:15,837 --> 00:12:18,705
What remains is not a
final picture to defend,

195
00:12:18,785 --> 00:12:21,042
but the freedom of not needing one.

196
00:12:21,122 --> 00:12:25,648
Each appearance is met as it
is. Vivid. Exact. Workable.

197
00:12:25,728 --> 00:12:28,220
Releasing itself as it arises.

198
00:12:29,041 --> 00:12:33,408
Light and complete, with nothing
to hold, and no one holding.

